{"attributes": {"type": "DifferentialExperiment", "particle": "decay", "reaction": "PFNS", "nuclide": "Cf-252", "library": "ARIADNE", "documentation": "EXFOR No. = 40874.004. Journal article =\nThe data from the group encompassing Starostov, Botsov and Nefedov~\\cite{Starostov1983, Botsov1983, Nefedov1983, Starostov1985} are stored in several EXFOR entries following the neutron detector used. Mannhart rejected the data but it is unclear why.\nData were taken in two cycles. For cycle 1, a miniaturized ionization chamber was used (98\\% efficiency), while cycle 2 used a gas scintillation detector (97\\% efficiency) to detect fission fragments. For cycle 1, an anthracene detector (height of 0.4 cm and diameter of 1.8 cm, TOF-path length: 51 cm) was used from 0.1--2 MeV, a stilbene scintillator (height of 3 cm and diameter of 7 cm, TOF-path length: 231.3 cm) from 1.4--8 MeV and a plastic scintillator (height of 12 cm and diameter of 20 cm, TOF-path length: 611 cm) from 3--12 MeV. They are stored in EXFOR sub-entries 40874.002, 40871.005 and 40872.002, respectively which had to be identified by their energy range. Data in 40874.003 and 40874.004 were measured in the second cycle preliminary with an ionization chamber from 0.01--5 MeV (height of 0.8 cm and diameter of 10 cm, TOF-path length: 12.4--40 cm, time resolution: 4.8 ns) and agas scintillation ionization chamber (height of 0.01 cm and diameter of 11 cm, TOF-path length: 10.4--29.5 cm, time resolution: 2.5 ns). The time resolution was 4.2 ns for cyle-1 measurements. The assumed Mawellian was 1.417 MeV. The neutron-detector response was simulated with $^1$H and $^{12}$C data for the anthracene detector. $^{252}$Cf data was used for the stilbene and plastic scintillator which is a circular argument, while $^{235}$U(n,) cross secitions were used to determine the neutron-detector efficiency of cycle-2 measurements.\nCorrections were described for many effects listed above; it is unknown if deadtime, sample decay, transmission through the shadow cone for background determination, and alpha background were accounted for in corrections. The anthracene and stilbene data agree with Mannhart evaluated data so well, and thus with the bulk of accepted experimental data that major corrections seem to have been correctly applied. Plastic data disagree noticeably.\nPartial uncertainties are provided for most major effects, counting statistics, background, multiple scattering, detector efficiency, and time resolution. TOF length uncertainties are also given and it is stated that corrections for angular distribution (and, hence, we assume the related uncertainties) are negigible. We take deadtime and impurity uncertainties from templates.\nThe data measured with the anthracene detector and in the second cycle (above 0.15 MeV) were accepted for obtaining a new evaluation of the $^{252}$Cf PFNS and ML. Stilbene and plastic data cannot be taken into account for both due to the circular assumption to define the detector efficiency.\n", "date": "2023-08-01", "Author": ["Boytsov", "Starostov"], "Year": "1983", "Facility": "N/A", "Institute": "4RUSNIR", "Isotope": "Cf-252", "Quantity": "PFNS", "MeasurementType": "PFNS", "ConcernEXFOR": "N/A", "ConcernAIACHNE": "Detector efficiency", "ConcernAIACHNE_text": "They used U-235(n,f) cs as monitor reaction for obtaining the detector efficiency that has structures below 150 keV. That is the energy range we cut it down to.", "BackgroundCorrected": "y", "AlphaBackground": "unknown", "GammaBackground": "y", "RandomCoincidenceBackground": "y", "ShadowBarBackground": "unknown", "WrapAroundBackground": "N/A", "MultipleScatteringSampleBackingCorrected": "y", "MultipleScatteringSurroundingCorrected": "y", "AttenuationSampleBackingCorrected": "y", "AttenuationSurroundingCorrected": "y", "FissionDetectionEfficiencyCorrected": "y", "NeutronDetectionEfficiencyCorrected": "y", "NeutronDetectionResponseCorrected": "y", "SampleDecayCorrected": "unknown", "FissionFragmentAbsorptioninSampleCorrected": "y", "SignalPulsePileupCorrected": "unknown", "DeadtimeCorrected": "unknown", "AngularDistributionFissionFragmentsCorrected": "y", "ImpuritiesCorrected": "unknown", "Mannhart": "n (unknown reason why not taken)", "CorrelatedData": ["40871.005", "40872.002", "40874.003", "40644.002", "40874.002"], "EXFORnumber": "40874.004", "Accepted": "y", "MissingCorrections": ["deadtime", "sampleDecay", "ShadowBarBackground", "AlphaBackground"], "FissionDetector": {"Type": "IOCH (Gas ionization detector)", "ParticleDetected": "FF", "Efficiency": 97.0, "EfficiencyMethod": ["sample roughness quantified", "Measured at different angle", "calculated"], "FFAbsorptionAngularDistributionMethod": ["sample roughness quantified", "calculated", "measured (at different angle)"], "AngularAcceptaneofFF": "unknown", "Gas": {"Type": "Methane", "Purity": "unknown", "Pressure": "unknown"}, "Size": {"geometry": "cylinder", "height": 3.8, "height_unit": "cm", "diameter": 3.8, "diameter_unit": "cm"}, "NoPhotomultipliers": "unknown", "Photomultipliers": "unknown", "Weight": "unknown", "StructuralMaterial": "Al", "ReferenceDetector": "N/A"}, "NeutronDetector": {"Type": "IOCH (Gas scintillation ionization detector)", "Number": "none", "ParticleDetected": "FF", "Efficiency": "unknown", "ResponseDeterminationMethod": "relative to U-235", "EfficiencyDeterminationMethod": "relative to U-235", "Angle": 0.0, "TOFLength": {"Value": 51.0, "Unit": "cm", "Unc": 1.0, "Unc_unit": "mm"}, "trsl": {"Value": 2.5, "Unit": "ns", "Measure": "FWHM"}, "t0Determination": ["calibrated delay line", "neutron transmission (252Cf)"], "Gas": {"Type": "unknown", "Purity": "unknown", "Pressure": "unknown"}, "Size": {"geometry": "cylinder", "diameter": 11.0, "diameter_unit": "cm", "height": 0.01, "height_unit": "cm"}, "NoPhotomultipliers": 1, "Photomultipliers": "unknown", "Weight": "unknown", "StructuralMaterial": ["U235"], "ReferenceDetector": "N/A", "ReferenceReaction": "235U(n,f) cs"}, "Shielding": {"M